---
// Privacy (sections 4.1 and 12): what is collected and by whom, in plain words.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { STATIC_PAGES } from "../lib/pages";
import { webPage } from "../lib/seo/jsonld";
import { canonicalUrl } from "../lib/seo/meta";

const page = STATIC_PAGES.privacy;
---

<Base
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  path={page.path}
  jsonLd={[
    webPage({
      url: canonicalUrl(page.path),
      title: page.title,
      description: page.description,
      dateModified: "2026-10-21",
    }),
  ]}
>
  <article class="wrap privacy">
    <header class="privacy__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>What this site collects</h1>
      <p class="privacy__lead measure">
        Short version: a contact message if you send one, an email address if you subscribe, and the
        usual visit counts through Google Analytics. Nothing is sold. Here is the long version.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy__sections">
      <section aria-labelledby="contact">
        <h2 id="contact">Contact messages</h2>
        <p>
          When you send a message through the contact form, I get it by email and a copy is stored
          in my Supabase database as a backup, with your name, your email address, the message, the
          time, a hashed form of your IP address used only to stop floods, and your browser's user
          agent string. It stays until I delete it. Ask and I will delete it sooner.
        </p>
        <p>
          The form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from scripts. Turnstile may set a cookie
          on its own domain while it runs; Cloudflare's privacy policy covers that.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="newsletter">
        <h2 id="newsletter">Newsletter</h2>
        <p>
          If you subscribe, your email address goes to Buttondown, which sends the letters, and a
          copy is kept in my database so Buttondown is not the only record. Every letter has an
          unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing removes you from both.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="analytics">
        <h2 id="analytics">Google Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          I use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages people read and which accessibility features
          they use, such as the screen reader view or the text size control. It sets cookies in your
          browser and sends page views, scrolls, outbound clicks and searches to Google, along with
          your rough location and your device type. It does not know who you are. I have turned off
          the advertising features and Google Signals, and nothing identifies you to me.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, analytics storage is off
          by default, so no cookie is set and the page view is counted without one. Anyone can opt
          out everywhere with the{" "}
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
          Vercel Speed Insights measures how fast pages load and stores nothing about you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="comments">
        <h2 id="comments">Comments</h2>
        <p>
          Comments run on Giscus, which uses GitHub Discussions. Nothing from Giscus loads until you
          choose to open the comments, and commenting means signing in to GitHub, whose terms then
          apply.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="settings">
        <h2 id="settings">Your settings</h2>
        <p>
          The theme and reading controls are stored in your browser's local storage, on your device
          only. They never leave it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="deletion">
        <h2 id="deletion">Asking for deletion</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="/contact?topic=privacy">Send me a message</a> and say what to delete. I will
          confirm when it is done.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <p class="privacy__updated mono">
      Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-21">2026-10-21</time>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-8);
  }
  .privacy__header h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .privacy__lead {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .privacy__sections {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .privacy__sections h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .privacy__sections p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .privacy__updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
</style>
